--TEST--
A second `sheet` finishes the first, so adding a row to the first throws naming it; a bad sheet name throws in `sheet` and the open sheet goes on; `position` sets the tab order; a row's `style` is a `Style` the workbook writes once; and `finish` counts the rows of each sheet: rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-writes-as-a-stream
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Workbook::sheet
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Sheet::add
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Style::of
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Style;
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Workbook;

var $book = Workbook::createInMemory();
var $bold = Style::of({bold: true, border: "thin", align: "center"});
var $orders = $book->sheet("Orders");
$orders->add(["Widget", 3], {style: $bold});
$orders->add(["Gadget", 4], {style: $bold});

// `Totals` comes first in the tabs, and starting it finishes `Orders`.
var $totals = $book->sheet("Totals", {position: 0});
$totals->add(["Sum", 7]);
try {
    $orders->add(["Gizmo", 5]);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// A sheet name cannot have `/`. `Totals` is still open after the error.
try {
    $book->sheet("Shop/Orders");
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
$totals->add(["Count", 2]);

// A style with a value that does not exist throws when you make it.
try {
    Style::of({border: "wavy"});
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

var $written = $book->finish();
echo "Orders: ", $written->rows["Orders"], ", Totals: ", $written->rows["Totals"], "\n";

bytes $file = $written->bytes ?? Core\Bytes::fill(0, 0);
var $workbook = Core\Zip::read($file, "xl/workbook.xml") as string;
echo Core\Str::contains($workbook, "<sheet name=\"Totals\" sheetId=\"2\" r:id=\"rId2\"/><sheet name=\"Orders\"") ? "Totals is the first tab" : "Orders is the first tab", "\n";

// Both rows use the same style, so `styles.xml` has it once.
var $sheet = Core\Zip::read($file, "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml") as string;
echo Core\Str::contains($sheet, "<row r=\"1\" s=\"1\" customFormat=\"1\">") ? "row 1 has the style" : "row 1 has no style", "\n";
echo Core\Str::contains($sheet, "<row r=\"2\" s=\"1\" customFormat=\"1\">") ? "row 2 has the same style" : "row 2 has another style", "\n";
var $styles = Core\Zip::read($file, "xl/styles.xml") as string;
echo Core\Str::contains($styles, "<cellXfs count=\"2\">") ? "one style and the default" : "another number of styles", "\n";
--EXPECT--
The sheet `Orders` is finished, so you cannot add rows to it. A sheet is finished when the workbook starts the next sheet.
The sheet name `Shop/Orders` has the character `/`. A sheet name cannot have `: \ / ? * [ ]`.
The style field `border` is `'thin'`, `'medium'`, `'thick'`, `'dashed'`, `'dotted'` or `'double'`. It has `'wavy'`.
Orders: 2, Totals: 2
Totals is the first tab
row 1 has the style
row 2 has the same style
one style and the default
